{{!-- The "Player moves" block shared by the threat and hazard cards. Invoked with the
      card view-model as context; renders nothing when there are no custom player moves.

      "Give to players" (GM-only, `canShare`) opens the custom-move editor filled in with this move,
      and saving makes it a world move the players can drag onto their sheets (Book I p.294 for a
      threat's player-facing moves; p.388 for a hazard's: "When the PCs encounter the hazard and the
      move becomes relevant, share it with the players"). Wired by threat-view.js
      #wireSharePlayerMoves in every host of the card. --}}
{{#if hasCustomMoves}}
<div class="threat-player-moves">
	<span class="threat-label">Player moves</span>
	{{#each customPlayerMoves}}
	<div class="threat-player-move">{{#if label}}<strong class="threat-player-move__name">{{label}}</strong>{{/if}}{{#if canShare}}<button type="button" class="threat-player-move__share" data-move-index="{{index}}" aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.threats.shareMove"}}" data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.threats.shareMoveTip"}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-share-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>{{/if}}<div class="threat-player-move__text">{{{text}}}</div></div>
	{{/each}}
</div>
{{/if}}
